Imagine you're at a restaurant, and you're waiting for your food. You're sitting at a table, and the waiter says, "We'll have your food ready soon." But if you suddenly get a call from your doctor saying you need to go to the hospital immediately, you can't just leave your seat and walk out—you still have to finish your meal, and the waiter has to know you're no longer waiting. So, you must tell the waiter you're leaving *before* you actually leave, and then you can go.  

