**Brief Plan:**

We implement a reader-preference readers-writers lock using a monitor pattern with a single mutex and two condition variables:  
- `can_read`: signals that a reader can enter (used by waiting readers).  
- `can_write`: signals that a writer can enter (used by waiting writers).  

The reader-preference rule means:  
- If there are waiting readers, they must be admitted before any writer.  
- During reading, readers must ensure no writer is active (mutual exclusion).  

We use a single mutex to protect shared state (reader count, writer active flag).  
- Readers increment a reader count and only allow reading if no writer is active.  
- Writers wait on `can_write` until no readers are active.  
- The monitor ensures mutual exclusion and progress:  
  - Readers can always proceed if any reader is active.  
  - Writers only proceed when no readers are active.  

We simulate 4 readers and 2 writers, each running 4 rounds (i.e., 4 times each), and terminate cleanly.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <pthread.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <time.h>

// Shared state
pthread_mutex_t mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
pthread_cond_t can_read = PTHREAD_COND_INITIALIZER;
pthread_cond_t can_write = PTHREAD_COND_INITIALIZER;

int reader_count = 0;
int writer_active = 0;

// Reader function
void* reader(void* arg) {
    int id = *(int*)arg;
    for (int round = 0; round < 4; round++) {
        printf("Reader %d: entering critical section (round %d)\n", id, round);

        // Acquire mutex to check writer activity and reader count
        pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);

        // Wait if there's a writer active
        while (writer_active) {
            pthread_cond_wait(&can_read, &mutex);
        }

        // Increment reader count
        reader_count++;

        // All readers are active now — no writer can enter
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);

        // Simulate reading
        usleep(100000); // 0.1 seconds

        // Exit section: decrement reader count
        pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);
        reader_count--;

        // If no readers are left, signal writers
        if (reader_count == 0) {
            pthread_cond_signal(&can_write);
        }
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);

        printf("Reader %d: exiting critical section (round %d)\n", id, round);
    }
    return NULL;
}

// Writer function
void* writer(void* arg) {
    int id = *(int*)arg;
    for (int round = 0; round <  4; round++) {
        printf("Writer %d: entering critical section (round %d)\n", id, round);

        pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);

        // Wait until no readers are active
        while (reader_count > 0) {
            pthread_cond_wait(&can_write, &mutex);
        }

        // Writer is active
        writer_active = 1;

        // Simulate writing
        usleep(100000); // 0.1 seconds

        writer_active = 0;
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);

        printf("Writer %d: exiting critical section (round %d)\n", id, round);
    }
    return NULL;
